<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37835" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαγλᾰΐζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>honour, grace,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆμον ὠφελίαισι βίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					575
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				682
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃν σοφίας μῦθος ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(9).954.7
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Chalcis</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.2532
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thebes</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>pride oneself on</i> a thing, <i>glory</i> or
				<i>exult in</i> it, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ ἕ φημι
				δηρὸν ἐπαγλαϊεῖσθαι</span> (fut.
			inf.) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.133
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπηγλαϊς μέναι . . τράπεζαι</span>”
				<i>dressed out,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					301
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
